# gc573-cap -R (returned-buffer test): ch0 CH_CTRL arming race, M2 review
# VM gc573-dev, kernel 6.8.0-151-generic, card fw 20200811, no HDMI input (M2: HDMI chips in
# reset, FPGA free-running at 60 Hz).
# Command: gc573-cap -d /dev/video0 -f NV12 -b 3 -R 200000 -D /sys/kernel/debug/gc573-0000:07:00.0/video
# before: module from c14e866 (M2 as merged): gc573_buf_queue() arms free slots whenever the
#         stream runs, a read-modify-write of ch0 CH_CTRL that can straddle a completion.
# after:  c14e866 + the fix (gc573_buf_queue() arms only when no slot is armed). Stopped by hand
#         after ~35500 QBUFs to free the card for M3 bring-up; debugfs at that point: frames 35474,
#         unarmed 0, order 0, bad_status 0, underruns 757.
# Result: the race did not reproduce: 200000 QBUFs at random times (3334 s), no write into a
# dequeued buffer, no completion for an unarmed slot. Bound (rule of three, 95 %): per-QBUF
# probability below 1.5e-5 under these conditions.

